nitely interests me loss was a  cultural phenomenon so when the show  ended many assumed the stars would go on  to even bigger things yet instead many  of them initially struggled Matthew  Fox's attempts to become a movie star  fizzled for instance while Josh Holloway  had  for old projects failed it got to the  point where some pundits joked that  there was a lost curse and de Ravin  wasn't immune her next project Americana  was passed over during pilot season part  of the issue  maybe that der Evan was typecast prior  to playing the pregnant Claire on lost  she also played a pregnant girl in the  film brick and went on to play another  pregnant character in the series Roswell  she told GQ I must have some sort of  maternal draw to me I do love children  but I don't really talk about that in  auditions hi I really love kids but me  but I keep reading scripts that are like  that too it's only fitting that de Ravin  eventually turned to fairytales to break  the curse in 2012 de Ravin join the cast  of Once Upon a Time which was created by  lost writers Edward kitsis and Adam  Horovitz she played Belle for seven  seasons on the hit show which is even  longer than she played Claire unlost  it's actually quite fabulous how as I'm  sure you know they sort of twist around  these fairy tale character she told The  Hollywood Reporter it was just a really  awesome journey to be able to give my  own spin on such a special icon ik  character and to work with such amazing  people de Ravin originally hails from  Australia I'm the only Australian who  loves peanut butter which led to a lot  of homesickness early in her career she  told the independent I don't get home as  much as I would like to I miss my family  so much  my ideal holiday is just to hang out  with them now though she has her own  family in America after divorcing her  first husband actor Josh Jana vets and  2014 de Ravin fell in love with the  submarine kid writer and director Erik  village they got engaged in 2016 the  same year Durov and gave birth to their  daughter Vera and in 2018 de Ravin  celebrated two new milestones she gave  birth to their son Theodore and she  officially became a US citizen you know  what they say home is where the heart is  in 2017 dear Evan told Entertainment  Weekly that she was finally taking some  time off work to focus on her new family  there are things in the works right now  but I've taken the last few  Soph to be a mom because I've been  working since I had a daughter a year  and a half ago so I was just very  excited to be able to do that since then  she's been true to her word with her  only recent project being the 2019 TV  movie a lover scorned it looks like this  phase of her career will be all about  finding a balance between work and  family but with two successful shows and  a few solid films under her belt de  Ravin still has a bright future in  Hollywood if and when she wants it check  out one of her newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite stars are coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

